  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner from Melton, Leicestershire, has died following an accident in Jordan on August 22. Lomas became paralysed from the chest down after a horse riding accident at the Osberton Horse Trials in 2007. Despite her disability, she raised nearly £1 million for charity by competing in various events using a bionic suit, including completing the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days and the Great North Run in 2016 while pregnant. She was also honored by lighting the Paralympic cauldron in Trafalgar Square in 2012. Her family has asked for privacy during this time."
